{
  "description": "The Admin API's project routes declare one generic 404 (`NotFound`) per operation, although the spec's own descriptions name which resource is missing: \"The project was not found.\" (getProject), \"The project or service account was not found.\" (service-account routes), \"The project or API key was not found.\" (getProjectApiKey), \"The project or pagination cursor was not found.\" (listProjectRateLimits). A missing project answers 404 `{ error: { code: \"project_not_found\", message: \"The project proj_abc was not found\", type: \"invalid_request_error\", param: null } }` (the spec's own example on GET /organization/projects/{project_id} and .../rate_limits). So: on the project-only routes (getProject, modifyProject, archiveProject) every 404 is ProjectNotFound; on the service-account routes and getProjectApiKey the 404 becomes ServiceAccountNotFound / ProjectApiKeyNotFound, while a body with `error.code: project_not_found` (two matcher fields, more specific) is ProjectNotFound. ServiceAccountNotFound/ProjectApiKeyNotFound replace NotFound in place, ahead of the appended ProjectNotFound, so a bare 404 ties to them by declaration order. The rate-limit routes keep NotFound (cursor / rate limit missing) and gain ProjectNotFound for the coded body only \u2014 the bare-404 matcher ties with the earlier NotFound and loses. Source: the OpenAPI spec descriptions and examples above; the Admin API could not be probed live (2026-10-06, no admin key).",
